Subject: [PATCH 06811/11362] wa30 L3 SOLVED: fence-socket relay, bank +1 level
 (70 -> 71)

Same agent (claude-fable-5) resumed with full L1/L2 context, asked to
attempt L3 without assuming the L2 solve structure (hand-carry +
open-room robot delivery) still applied. Found the dashed fence
splitting the map is not a barrier to remove but a two-sided socket:
a carried block dropped into a fence tile from the player's side is
autonomously extracted and delivered by the robot from the other
side. Workers never share a side, so no pathing collisions. Solved in
a single continuous episode, 340/400 step budget, 0 game-overs.

Independently re-verified before accepting (same protocol as the L2
breakthrough): extracted the artifact's 170-action sequence and ran
arc_solver_kit.reproduce() myself from 5 fresh env.reset() calls.
All 5 returned reached_level=3, reproduced=True, matching the
artifact's self-reported checksum. Mechanical
arc-reproduced-count-integrity-lint passes against the updated
counters.

levels_reproduced 2 -> 3 for wa30; reproducible_total_levels 70 -> 71.
Bonus L4 recon noted (three robots, maze walls, central fenced
enclosure) for a future attempt -- not itself attempted this round.

